# Copy this file to security/privacy-denylist.local (git ignores that name) and list the real
# names that must never appear in a file or commit message: account folder, character names,
# realm, computer username, and so on. One per line; matching ignores case. Lines starting
# with # are comments.
#
# The privacy scan, the git hooks and scripts/check.sh read the .local file. It is never
# committed, so the names stay on your machine. CI does not have it; the generic rules in
# scripts/privacy_scan.sh still run there.
#
# Examples (placeholders, replace them):
# MyAccountName
# MyMainCharacter
# my-computer-username
